+- Runtimes that load guests are web, desktop, and mobile (hosted and Capacitor); VS Code marks the catalog `unsupported`. The phone mounts extension panels as workspace drawer tabs and `contributes.statusSection` sections in its Status tab, and Settings → Extensions is offered there; `contributes.integration` account cards stay off the phone, which connects accounts from web or desktop like the tracker and notification-channel cards. Pages, attach rows, actions, commands, `@` mentions, chat blocks, tool presentations and file editors stay on web and desktop, and `openSurface`, `openCommit` and popovers answer `UNSUPPORTED` in a phone-mounted frame. A panel's service runs on the connected server, never on the phone.
+
 Notification services can receive kind `pull-request` for a GitHub merge the user requested here. It carries no session identity. The fixed event title and repository reference use the ordinary notification text fields; enterprise mode strips the reference at the host boundary. Services that validate notification kinds with an older SDK must update that parser to accept this additive kind.
 
 - `scripts/bump-version.mjs` refreshes `bun.lock` after bumping package versions; include both in the release commit. Bun resolves `workspace:*` in published archives from lockfile versions, and a frozen install can succeed with stale versions. `scripts/bump-version.test.mjs` covers the bump, frozen install, and packed dependency versions together.
 
 - Extension activity uses `useConfigStore.isConnected` plus live status records and directory `sessionStatusReady` authority. `useUIStore.eventStreamStatus` is an unmaintained diagnostic field, not a connection gate; its default `idle` must not hide known running or idle sessions as `unknown`.
 
-- `contributes.statusSection` is `true` or `{ entry?, source?, title?, height?, defaultExpanded?, requiresProject? }` (`StatusSectionContribution`), the object form with `entry`, `source`, or both. `true` reuses `panel.entry` and fails as `invalid-status-section` without one; the object form's `entry` is package-local `.html`, `title` 1 to `GUEST_STATUS_SECTION_TITLE_MAX` (60), `height` `GUEST_STATUS_SECTION_HEIGHT_MIN`..`MAX` (24..320). `defaultExpanded` defaults to true and only applies when the user has no saved expansion choice. `requiresProject` defaults to false; when true, the actual Work Status directory controls both presence and body rendering. `resolveStatusSectionEntry` resolves shorthand. The object form is a frame of its own: without `panel.entry` or `background.entry` it permits `capabilities`, `service`, `integration`, and `filesystem`, and refuses `page`, `attach`, `actions`, and `commands` as `invalid-panel`, because those are opened or invoked elsewhere. The server validates the HTML/scripts, exposes `statusEntry`/`statusTitle`/`statusHeight`, and counts `statusEntry` as a runtime entry for serving and storage. The host mounts `PluginPane surface="status"` inside the Work Status panel (`components/chat/work-status/WorkStatusExtensionSection.tsx`, see that folder's `DOCUMENTATION.md`): the same sandbox, guest-scoped token, context, grants, approval, and pause gates as a panel. Guest `resize` (`host.setHeight`, `ResizeRequest { height }`, integer 0..`GUEST_FRAME_HEIGHT_MAX`) is a request answered with an empty result on every surface; only `status` sizes its frame from it, through `clampStatusSectionHeight`, and a page docked to a shared surface sizes its dock from it (`DockedGuestPage` in `ContextPanel`: thickness across the dock edge, at least `GUEST_SURFACE_DOCK_SIZE_MIN`, at most half the panel through CSS). Each frame's `setHeight` reaches only its own pane. A status frame never registers a command resolver, clears a badge, or closes rail tabs